  "introText": "A 401(k) and a 529 plan do different jobs: the 401(k) is for your own retirement and the 529 is for a student's education costs, so they are not interchangeable and money in one cannot simply be moved to the other. At ModernWallet, we review account structures to help families map their cash flow across competing long-term goals without triggering avoidable penalties. Which account gets your next dollar depends on which goal arrives first, how the tax treatment fits your household income, and what access you need before retirement age. Every dollar placed into a 529 plan must follow rules governing qualified educational expenses, while money in a workplace retirement plan remains bound by federal retirement distribution age thresholds.",
